  "definitions": "Unified primary metrics (Papers A and B, 2026-11-13) from timed runner rows (rows_*.jsonl).\n\nM1  worst-user spectral efficiency F(b) = min_k R_k(b), bit/s/Hz, of the returned action, rescored under the\n    stored precoder (the RZF precoder of the all-OFF channel). Frames and seeds are averaged within a trajectory,\n    then over trajectories (the unit of the frozen analysis).\nM2  optimisation latency, ms = search_elapsed_ms (evaluator build + search, including selector features and\n    neural inference; stopped before the rescoring check). Mean, median and p95 over all calls.\nM3  computational budget = the hard deadline (5 / 10 / 50 / 100 ms; 50 ms primary) plus the number of candidate\n    evaluations used (`evaluations`: one per candidate configuration whose objective was scored, exact low-rank or\n    full, as counted by each solver). Mean, median and p95 over all calls.\nSecondary: miss fraction on the search clock (0.5% rule), mean selector ms, the rescoring-inclusive clock."
